{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The short Ethernet cables fit my recent effort to improve wired connections and organize my setup; they serve a different purpose from the five-foot cables I already bought.",
    "The memory card and reader connect to my Raspberry Pi and removable-storage purchases, making them useful additions if compatibility checks out."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming players and Alexa devices do not address my current computer, networking, or maintenance needs; buying electronics does not mean I am setting up a connected home.",
    "The HDMI cable repeats a need I have already filled, while the large internal SSD assumes an upgrade project and compatible computer that I have not identified."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics seems to have been treated as interest in TV streaming and voice-controlled devices.",
    "My cable and memory-card purchases seem to have been interpreted as reasons to suggest more cables or larger storage, without enough attention to their specific uses."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet adapter, cable, headphone mount, and duster purchases point toward improving connectivity, organization, and upkeep of my existing setup.",
    "I care about whether an accessory adds a useful capability, fits my equipment, and meets an unresolved need rather than duplicating something I already have."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my networking and Raspberry Pi interests but stretched them into streaming, home automation, and upgrades I do not currently need."
}"}
